# Skill: kickoff

Cursor adapter for the `kickoff` skill. Full procedure (single source of truth):
`.claude/skills/kickoff/SKILL.md` in this repo.

## When To Use

The user is about to `/clear` and wants a self-contained prompt to resume the paper work in a new
session. This repo has one context: finishing the HESS dataset paper.

## When Not To Use

Persisting session state (use `/handoff` or `/save`); executing a plan right now.

## Workflow

Point at the most recent committed plan/doc if one exists, else reconstruct the resume point from
`git log` + open todos + manuscript state. Verify the branch and clean/pushed state from git — never
guess. Check `git -C paper/overleaf status -s`; commit + push any referenced artifact (including the
submodule pointer) first so a fresh session can see it.

## Output Handling

Output only the paste-ready prompt in a code block, then one line noting anything committed/pushed to
make it durable. Reference artifacts; don't inline them. Include "already done" so work isn't redone.

## Safety Constraints

Do not auto-commit beyond what's needed to make referenced artifacts visible, and confirm with the
user before pushing. Verify every concrete fact from the repo, not from recall.
